# Copy to dev/site.env (git-ignored) and fill in your lab; `make dev-api` loads it.
# `make dev-api` points KUBECONFIG at the lab's kubeconfig. DASH_DEV no longer sends upstream URLs
# through the API server: the next line does, so the monitoring services below can use their
# in-cluster addresses. A source left out is "not configured".
DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_UPSTREAM_VIA_API_SERVER=true
# The kubeconfig context to use (empty: the kubeconfig's current one).
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_CONTEXT=lab
# Mount the workload Restart action (off by default).
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_ACTIONS_ENABLED=true
# Namespace labels dash reads (empty: the feature is off): a protected namespace asks you to type
# its name before a restart, a tenant label groups namespaces, a Flux Kustomization prefix marks Apps.
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_CONVENTIONS_PROTECTED_LABEL=example.com/protected
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_CONVENTIONS_TENANT_LABEL=example.com/tenant
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_CONVENTIONS_APPS_FLUX_PREFIX=apps-
# Flux: the annotation whose value is shown as the reason an object is suspended (empty: none),
# sources that must be signed and verified (a GitRepository or OCIRepository with spec.verify is
# checked anyway), and the Reconcile action (off by default).
# DASH_PLUGINS_FLUX_SUSPEND_REASON_ANNOTATION=example.com/suspended
# DASH_PLUGINS_FLUX_VERIFY_SOURCES='[{"kind":"GitRepository","namespace":"gitops","name":"fleet"}]'
# DASH_PLUGINS_FLUX_ACTIONS_ENABLED=true
# The CronJobs behind the backup ages, up to 8 (label names the row).
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_BACKUP_JOBS='[{"namespace":"backup","cronjob":"nightly","label":"Nightly"}]'
# Which routes are apps (empty accepts every HTTPRoute) and which namespaces never are.
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_APPS_GATEWAYS='[{"namespace":"gateways","name":"main"}]'
# DASH_PLUGINS_KUBERNETES_APPS_EXCLUDE_NAMESPACES='["dash"]'
DASH_PLUGINS_PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring.svc:9090
DASH_PLUGINS_ALERTMANAGER_URL=http://alertmanager.monitoring.svc:9093
DASH_PLUGINS_VICTORIALOGS_URL=http://victorialogs.monitoring.svc:9428
DASH_PLUGINS_GATUS_URL=http://gatus.gatus.svc:8080
DASH_PLUGINS_PROXMOX_URL=https://pve.example.com:8006
DASH_PLUGINS_PROXMOX_NODE=pve
# A self-signed Proxmox certificate: trust its CA (or, for a throwaway lab only, skip verification).
# DASH_PLUGINS_PROXMOX_TLS_CA_FILE=/path/to/pve-ca.pem
# A stopped VM with one of these ids or tags is critical, any other stopped VM is a warning.
# DASH_PLUGINS_PROXMOX_CRITICAL_VMS_IDS='[101]'
# DASH_PLUGINS_PROXMOX_CRITICAL_VMS_TAGS='["prod"]'
# Where the storage list comes from: api (default) or prometheus.
# DASH_PLUGINS_PROXMOX_STORAGE_SOURCE=api
# The host behind the cluster: its model, drive bays and the top of the fan gauges (0 derives both
# from what the host reports). Its node is the running Proxmox plugin's (it needs the URL, token ID and
# token secret) unless `nodename` is set.
DASH_PLUGINS_HARDWARE_HOSTS='[{"model":"Example 2U","bays":16,"fanMaxRPM":18000}]'
# Machines outside the cluster, shown as up or down: by their node-exporter or by a Gatus check.
# DASH_PLUGINS_HARDWARE_MACHINES='[{"name":"nas","nodeExporterNodename":"nas"},{"name":"pi","gatusEndpoint":"pi SSH"}]'
# The ZFS scrub series (a textfile collector's prefix); empty queries none.
# DASH_PLUGINS_HARDWARE_ZFS_SCRUB_METRIC_PREFIX=example_zfs_scrub
DASH_PLUGINS_HEADLAMP_URL=https://headlamp.example.com
DASH_PLUGINS_GRAFANA_URL=https://grafana.example.com
# A launcher file like docs/launcher.example.yaml; dev/launcher.yaml is git-ignored too.
DASH_PLUGINS_LAUNCHER_FILE=dev/launcher.yaml
# Icon names (proxmox, idrac, ...) need an icon base, for launcher links and for the apps on the
# Apps page; without it both show letter tiles.
DASH_UI_ICON_BASE_URL=https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/homarr-labs/dashboard-icons/png
